cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Ghost Scale Simulation
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite both this repository and
  the companion preprint.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Haskins
    given-names: Abraham
repository-code: "https://github.com/EmotiveAutomaton/ghost-scale-sim"
abstract: >-
  A working model of how people work out what someone was trying to do when they
  made something, what breaks when nothing was trying to do anything, and
  whether a label saying "this was generated" helps. Technically: an
  active-inference simulation in which an observer infers the goal behind an
  artifact, the artifact may have been produced by a process whose goal lies
  outside the observer's hypothesis space, and an honest or dishonest provenance
  signal conditions the inference. Includes a validation pass that re-runs the
  headline results under exact rather than approximate inference and measures the
  apparatus's own false-positive rate. Companion code to "Art as an Algorithmic
  Virus".
keywords:
  - active-inference
  - theory-of-mind
  - ai-provenance
  - ai-disclosure
  - model-collapse
  - computational-model
  - simulation
  - pomdp
  - reproducibility
  - preregistration
